# /new-ui-surface -- Add a UI Surface ({{ ui }})

## What This Does

Creates an HTML entrypoint in `entrypoints/` with a {{ app }} mounted into it, reading
state through `utils/storage.ts` and calling the background through `utils/messaging.ts`.
WXT turns the folder into the manifest entry; nothing is hand-written in `manifest.json`.
Follow `.claude/styles/{{ style_file }}.md` and `.claude/patterns/{{ 'patterns/ui-surfaces.md' | installed(stack) }}`.

## Usage

```
/new-ui-surface options          # entrypoints/options/   -> options_ui
/new-ui-surface sidepanel        # entrypoints/sidepanel/ -> side_panel (Chrome) / sidebar_action (Firefox)
/new-ui-surface popup            # entrypoints/popup/     -> action.default_popup
/new-ui-surface newtab           # entrypoints/newtab/    -> chrome_url_overrides.newtab
```

## Steps

### 1. Files

```
entrypoints/<surface>/
  index.html       # <div id="app"> + <script type="module" src="./{{ main }}">
  {{ main }}{{ ' ' * (17 - main | length) }}# mounts the app
{% if ui == 'React' %}
  App.tsx
{% elif ui == 'Vue' %}
  App.vue
{% elif ui == 'Svelte' %}
  App.svelte
{% endif %}
  style.css
```

Manifest options go in `<meta>` tags of `index.html`, e.g.
`<meta name="manifest.open_in_tab" content="true" />` (options as a full tab) or
`<meta name="manifest.open_at_install" content="true" />` (side panel).

### 2. Mount

{% if ui == 'React' %}
```tsx
// entrypoints/options/main.tsx
import { StrictMode } from 'react';
import { createRoot } from 'react-dom/client';
import App from './App';
import './style.css';

createRoot(document.getElementById('app')!).render(
  <StrictMode>
    <App />
  </StrictMode>,
);
```
{% elif ui == 'Vue' %}
```typescript
// entrypoints/options/main.ts
import { createApp } from 'vue';
import App from './App.vue';
import './style.css';

createApp(App).mount('#app');
```
{% elif ui == 'Svelte' %}
```typescript
// entrypoints/options/main.ts
import { mount } from 'svelte';
import App from './App.svelte';
import './style.css';

mount(App, { target: document.getElementById('app')! });
```
{% else %}
```typescript
// entrypoints/options/main.ts -- build nodes, set textContent, never innerHTML with data
import { settings, type Settings } from '@/utils/storage';

const app = document.querySelector<HTMLDivElement>('#app')!;
const enabled = document.createElement('input');
enabled.type = 'checkbox';
app.replaceChildren(enabled);

const render = (s: Settings) => (enabled.checked = s.enabled);
enabled.addEventListener('change', async () =>
  settings.setValue({ ...(await settings.getValue()), enabled: enabled.checked }),
);
settings.watch(render);
settings.getValue().then(render);
```
{% endif %}

### 3. Data

- Settings and shared state: a `storage.defineItem` in `utils/storage.ts` (`/new-storage-item`),
{% if ui == 'React' %}
  read through the `useStorageItem` hook (`.claude/styles/{{ 'styles/ui-react.md' | installed(stack) }}` section 2).
{% elif ui == 'Vue' %}
  read through the `useStorageItem` composable (`.claude/styles/{{ 'styles/ui-vue.md' | installed(stack) }}` section 2).
{% elif ui == 'Svelte' %}
  read through `storageState()` from `lib/storage-state.svelte.ts` (`.claude/styles/{{ 'styles/ui-svelte.md' | installed(stack) }}` section 2).
{% else %}
  rendered in a `watch` callback so every surface stays in sync.
{% endif %}
- Privileged work (tabs, network with host permissions): a typed message to the background
  (`/new-message`), never `browser.*` calls duplicated in the surface.

### 4. Surface specifics

- **options**: open it from code with `browser.runtime.openOptionsPage()`.
- **sidepanel**: WXT writes `side_panel` (Chrome) / `sidebar_action` (Firefox). Chrome also
  needs the `sidePanel` permission: check the built manifest and add it to
  `manifest.permissions` in `wxt.config.ts` if missing. To open it from the toolbar icon:
  `browser.sidePanel.setPanelBehavior({ openPanelOnActionClick: true })` in the background,
  guarded with `if (!import.meta.env.FIREFOX)`. `sidePanel.open()` only works in a user gesture.
- **popup**: fixed `body` width (e.g. 360px); it is destroyed on close, so no timers or
  in-memory state.
- **newtab**: loads on every new tab; keep it fast (no blocking network on first paint).

### 5. Test

- Unit: logic in `utils/` with Vitest + `fakeBrowser` (`/test`).
- E2E: one Playwright spec that opens `chrome-extension://${extensionId}/<surface>.html`
  (`.claude/patterns/{{ 'patterns/testing.md' | installed(stack) }}`, section 7), e.g. `options.html`, `sidepanel.html`.

### 6. Verify

```bash
npm run compile
npm run build      # check .output/{{ variables.target_browser }}-mv3/manifest.json has the new entry
```

## Checklist

- [ ] Folder entrypoint with `index.html` + `{{ main }}`; manifest options in `<meta>` tags
- [ ] State via `utils/storage.ts` items, privileged calls via `utils/messaging.ts`
- [ ] Page and user data rendered as text, never as HTML
- [ ] Side panel: `sidePanel` permission present for Chrome; Firefox path checked
- [ ] `npm run compile` and `npm run build` pass; E2E spec opens the page
